IMPORT prelude

-- Health Services Act 2016 (WA) -- what a WA public hospital may charge the patient. Is the care a public health service in a
-- public hospital (ss 7, 8); may the health service provider charge me at all, and within what limits (ss 54, 55, 56); who
-- owes the fee and whether it can be waived (s 57); when a hospital can take its charge out of my compensation (ss 53A, 53B,
-- 57A, 57C, 57D); and the patient-facing duties the Act states (a complaints procedure, s 34(2)(f); confidentiality of my
-- information, ss 217, 219, 220). The amounts come from the Health Services (Fees and Charges) Order 2016, made under s 56:
-- my class of patient (Order Part 3), what I am charged per day as an in-patient, day patient or same day patient, per
-- out-patient service, for out-patient medicines, for an MRI study and for pathology, and what someone staying with me pays
-- (Order cll 3, 3A, 5, 6, 6A, 7, 8, 10A, 11-15 and Schedule 1 Divisions 1-4).
--
-- SEAT: the public patient -- "What does the public hospital charge me?". Every exported question is the patient's: "Is my
-- care a public health service?", "Is this a public hospital?", "May the hospital charge me at all?", "What class of patient
-- am I?", "What does the hospital charge me per day?", "What will my stay cost?", "What do I pay for an out-patient visit, a
-- medicine, an MRI, a pathology test?", "Can the hospital recover its charge out of my compensation?", "Must the hospital
-- have a complaints procedure?", "May my health information be disclosed?". The comparison the seat asks for -- a
-- Medicare-eligible public patient against a private patient and against a person who is not Medicare-eligible -- is the
-- class of patient, which the Order works out from facts the patient can state. Where the Act or the Order hands a judgment
-- to someone else (the chief executive deciding I am no longer compensable, Order cl 3A(5); the chief executive's opinion
-- under s 217; a waiver under s 57(2); whether the National Health Agreement says I am not to be charged, s 55(1)(a)), it is
-- asked as a fact.
--
-- Provisions covered: Act ss 5, 7(3), (4), 8(4), (6)-(8), 34(2)(f), 53A, 53B, 54, 55, 56(2) (its effect), 57, 57A(1)-(3),
-- 57C, 57D, 217, 219(1), (2), 220(1). Order cl 3(1) ("asylum seeker", "eligible person", "Medicare ineligible asylum
-- seeker", "Medicare ineligible involuntary patient"), cl 3(3) (as a fact), cl 3A(1)-(5), cll 5, 6, 6A, 7, 8, 10A, 11-15,
-- Schedule 1 Division 1 items 1-7, Division 2 items 1-10, Division 3, Division 4.
--
-- Edition: the compilation of the Health Services Act 2016 retrieved on 7 September 2026 (mrdoc 48912), whose compilation
-- table ends with the Industrial Relations Legislation Amendment Act 2024 (in operation 31 January 2025) and lists the
-- Evidence Act 2025 s 492(1) as uncommenced, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_48912.txt. Order: the
-- Health Services (Fees and Charges) Order 2016, consolidated version 00-aw0-00, currency start 1 July 2026 (includes the
-- Health Services (Fees and Charges) Amendment Order (No. 2) 2026, SL 2026/142), as deposited at
-- ../../../health-services-fees-and-charges-order-2016/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49652.txt. NOT DEPOSITED: the National
-- Health Reform Agreement (s 6 "National Health Agreement"), the regulations made under the Act, the policy frameworks under
-- s 26(2)(e), the Medicare Benefits Schedule (so every MBS amount is an INPUT) and the Department CEO's at-cost
-- determinations under Order cll 9 and 10A.
--
-- AMOUNTS AS PRINTED. Every dollar figure is the Order's figure in force from 1 July 2026. The Order is amended about twice a
-- year; a 2030 or 2063 event is answered under the 2026 figures.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the machinery (Parts 2, 3, 5, 7-16, 18, 19; boards, chief executives, employment, discipline, inquiries,
-- transfers, land); s 59 (fees for things that are not health services); the compensable-charge regulations (s 58), the
-- apportionment and review they may provide, and s 57B (services of a former public hospital before 1 July 2016); Order
-- cl 9 (specialised orthoses, at cost) and cl 10 and Schedule 1 Division 6 (surgically implanted prostheses); the Department
-- CEO's own charges (s 23(3)); whether a person "resides" or holds a visa, and so whether they are an "eligible person" under
-- the Health Insurance Act 1973 (borrowed: see that Act's baseline); what doctors charge privately (the Health Insurance Act
-- and its s 128C); the Mental Health Act 2014 orders that make a person an involuntary patient (a fact).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Health Services Act 2016 -- what the public hospital may charge me`

§§ `ss 7, 8 -- is my care a public health service, in a public hospital`

-- s 7(1): "A health service is a service for maintaining, improving, restoring or managing people's physical and mental health
-- and wellbeing." s 7(3): "A public health service is a health service provided by -- (a) a health service provider; or (b)
-- the Department CEO; or (c) a contracted health entity under a contract or other agreement entered into with -- (i) a health
-- service provider; or (ii) the Department CEO, the Minister or the Premier on behalf of the State." s 7(4): it "(a) includes
-- a health service declared under a regulation to be a public health service; and (b) does not include a health service
-- declared under a regulation not to be a public health service."
-- Glosses: a "health service provider" is one of the WA health services (the area health services) established by order
-- under s 32(1)(b); a "contracted health entity" is a non-government entity providing health services to the State under
-- contract (s 6).
DECLARE `Who provides my health service` IS ONE OF
    `a health service provider`
    `the Department CEO`
    `a contracted health entity under a contract with a health service provider or the State`
    `a private provider with no such contract`

@export Is my care a public health service (s 7(3), (4))?
GIVEN `provider` IS A `Who provides my health service` @desc Who gives you the care
      `declared public by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation declares this service to be a public health service
      `declared not public by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a regulation declares this service not to be a public health service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my care a public health service` IF
        (NOT `declared not public by regulation`)
    AND (    `declared public by regulation`
         OR  CONSIDER `provider`
             WHEN `a private provider with no such contract` THEN FALSE
             OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 8(4): a "hospital" is premises where "medical, surgical or dental treatment, or nursing care, is provided for ill or
-- injured persons and at which overnight accommodation may be provided", a day hospital facility, or a nursing post.
-- s 8(6): "Subject to any order made under subsection (8), each of the following premises is a public hospital ... (a) a
-- hospital controlled or managed by a health service provider or the Department CEO; or (b) a hospital declared to be a
-- public hospital under subsection (7)." (8): the Minister may by order declare that "any hospital is not a public hospital".
@export Is the hospital a public hospital (s 8(6)-(8))?
GIVEN `controlled or managed by a health service provider or the Department CEO` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a WA health service provider or the Department runs the hospital
      `declared a public hospital by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order in the Gazette declares it a public hospital (s 8(7))
      `declared not a public hospital by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Ministerial order in the Gazette declares it not a public hospital (s 8(8))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the hospital a public hospital` IF
        (NOT `declared not a public hospital by the Minister`)
    AND (`controlled or managed by a health service provider or the Department CEO` OR `declared a public hospital by the Minister`)

§§ `ss 5, 54, 55, 56 -- may the hospital charge me at all`

-- s 5: "The provision of health services through the public hospital system of the State is based on the Medicare principles
-- set out in the National Health Agreement." s 54: the Minister and providers "must have regard to the National Health
-- Agreement". Neither gives the patient a right in terms; s 55 is where the Agreement bites.
-- s 55(1): "A health service provider may determine and impose a fee or charge for the provision of a health service by the
-- health service provider unless the service is -- (a) a health service provided to a person in respect of which it has been
-- agreed under the National Health Agreement that the person is not to be charged, but only if the Agreement is in force at
-- the time the service is provided; or (b) a health service in respect of which the Minister has made an order under section
-- 56(2)(b), but only if the order is in force at the time the service is provided."
-- s 56(2): the Minister may by order "(a) fix fees and charges ...; and (b) provide that no fees or charges are payable in
-- respect of -- (i) a specified health service or class of health service; or (ii) a health service rendered to a specified
-- class of patient; or (iii) a health service in respect of any specified public hospital or class of public hospital." The
-- Order's cl 6A is such a provision.
-- The National Health Agreement (the National Health Reform Agreement of 2 August 2011 or its successor, s 6) is NOT DEPOSITED,
-- so whether it says I am not to be charged is a fact.
@export May the health service provider charge me for my health service at all (s 55(1))?
GIVEN `provider` IS A `Who provides my health service` @desc Who gives you the care
      `the National Health Agreement says I am not to be charged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has been agreed under the National Health Agreement that you are not to be charged for this service
      `the Agreement is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the National Health Agreement is in force when the service is given
      `a Ministerial order says no fees are payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order under s 56(2)(b) in force when the service is given says no fees or charges are payable for it (for example Order cl 6A)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the hospital charge me at all` IF
        (CONSIDER `provider`
         WHEN `a health service provider` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (NOT (`the National Health Agreement says I am not to be charged` AND `the Agreement is in force`))
    AND (NOT `a Ministerial order says no fees are payable`)

§§ `Order cll 3, 3A, 11-15 -- what class of patient am I`

-- Order cl 3(1): "eligible person has the meaning given in the Health Insurance Act 1973 (Commonwealth) section 3" (including a
-- person to be treated as one, excluding a person to be treated as not one). Borrowed, so asked as a fact: the Health Insurance
-- Act 1973 baseline works it out.
-- "asylum seeker means a person -- (a) who has applied for -- (i) a permanent protection visa ...; or (ii) a temporary
-- protection visa ...; or (iii) a safe haven enterprise visa ...; and (b) whose visa application ... has not yet been decided".
-- "Medicare ineligible asylum seeker means a person who -- (a) is an asylum seeker; and (b) is not an eligible person; and (c)
-- is not a compensable patient". "Medicare ineligible involuntary patient" likewise, for an "involuntary patient" (cl 3(3): a
-- person under an inpatient or community treatment order, or another detaining order, or an unexpired referral, under the
-- Mental Health Act 2014 -- asked as a fact).
-- Order cl 3A(1)-(4): a compensable day patient, in-patient, out-patient or same day patient is one "who -- (i) has received or
-- established a right to receive compensation in respect of an injury, illness or disease for which the patient is receiving
-- health services; or (ii) when attending a hospital appears prima facie to have the right to receive compensation ...; and
-- (b) in relation to whom a decision under subclause (5) has not been made". A compensable same day patient must also be "an
-- eligible person" (cl 3A(4)(a)). cl 3A(5): the chief executive "may decide that the patient is not a compensable patient" if
-- satisfied the compensation is spent, the right has gone, the patient "would be unfairly disadvantaged", or it is not in the
-- provider's interest -- asked as a fact.
-- cll 12(3), 13(3), 14(5), 15(5): each compensable class "includes a person in respect of the payment for whose health services
-- one or more of the following applies or appears prima facie to apply -- (a) the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act
-- 2023; (ab) the Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016; (b) the Motor Vehicle (Third Party
-- Insurance) Act 1943; (c) the law of Australia relating to the Defence Force". These "includes" limbs carry no cl 3A(5)
-- condition.
DECLARE `My election` IS ONE OF
    `to be a public patient`
    `to be a private patient`

DECLARE `Me as a patient` HAS
    `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 3(1), borrowed
    `I have, or appear to have, a right to compensation for this condition`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 3A(1)-(4)(a)
    `the chief executive has decided I am not a compensable patient`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 3A(5)
    `motor vehicle third party insurance applies or appears to apply`             IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 12(3)(b) etc.; Sch 1 Div 2 items 2, 3, 10
    `workers compensation, catastrophic injuries or Defence Force law applies or appears to apply` IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 12(3)(a), (ab), (c) etc.
    `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement`                                IS A BOOLEAN  -- cll 12(2)(d), 14(2)(b), 15(2)(d)
    `I am a nursing home type patient`                                             IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 12(2)(e), (f); Health Insurance Act term
    `my election`                                                                  IS A `My election`  -- cll 12(4), 15(3)
    `I am an asylum seeker`                                                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 3(1)
    `I am an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2014`                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 3(3)
    `the service is part of my Mental Health Act treatment`                        IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 6A(b), 11(2)(b)
    `a declaration under s 6(2) of the Health Insurance Act 1973 applies to me`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- cl 12(2)(g)(i)

-- cl 11(1): a patient "must be classified as -- (a) an in-patient [admitted ... to receive health services in a hospital bed];
-- or (b) a day patient, namely, a person who receives health services at a day hospital; or (c) an out-patient [attending an
-- out-patient service, or served by the hospital elsewhere]; or (d) a same day patient, namely, a person who is admitted to
-- and discharged from a hospital, not being a day hospital, nursing home or a nursing post, between midnight on one day and
-- midnight on the next".
DECLARE `How I attend` IS ONE OF
    `as an in-patient`
    `as a day patient`
    `as an out-patient`
    `as a same day patient`

DECLARE `My class` IS ONE OF
    `a public in-patient`
    `a private in-patient`
    `a compensable in-patient`
    `an eligible veteran in-patient`
    `a nursing home type patient`
    `a nursing home type private patient`
    `an ineligible in-patient`
    `a compensable day patient`
    `an eligible day patient`
    `an ineligible day patient`
    `a compensable out-patient`
    `an eligible veteran out-patient`
    `an eligible out-patient`
    `an ineligible out-patient`
    `a public same day patient`
    `a private same day patient`
    `a compensable same day patient`
    `an eligible veteran same day patient`
    `an ineligible same day patient`
    `not classified: no fees or charges are payable (cl 6A)`
    `not classified: the Order gives no in-patient class`

@export Am I a compensable patient (Order cll 3A, 12(3), 13(3), 14(5), 15(5))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a compensable patient` IF
        `me`'s `motor vehicle third party insurance applies or appears to apply`
    OR  `me`'s `workers compensation, catastrophic injuries or Defence Force law applies or appears to apply`
    OR  (    `me`'s `I have, or appear to have, a right to compensation for this condition`
         AND (NOT `me`'s `the chief executive has decided I am not a compensable patient`)
         AND CONSIDER `attending`
             WHEN `as a same day patient` THEN `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973`
             OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- cl 6A: "Despite any other provision of this Part, no fees or charges are payable in respect of a health service provided to --
-- (a) a Medicare ineligible asylum seeker; or (b) a Medicare ineligible involuntary patient as part of their treatment under the
-- Mental Health Act 2014." cl 11(2): such a patient "does not need to be classified".
@export Am I free of all hospital fees and charges as a Medicare-ineligible asylum seeker or involuntary patient (Order cl 6A)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I free of all fees under cl 6A` IF
        (NOT `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973`)
    AND (NOT (`Am I a compensable patient` `me` `attending`))
    AND (    `me`'s `I am an asylum seeker`
         OR  (`me`'s `I am an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2014` AND `me`'s `the service is part of my Mental Health Act treatment`))

-- cl 12(2): an in-patient is "(a) a public in-patient, namely, an in-patient -- (i) who is an eligible person (not being a
-- compensable in-patient, nursing home type patient or nursing home type private patient, or an in-patient who elects to be
-- treated as a private in-patient); and (ii) who elects to be treated as a public in-patient; and (iii) [who is given] in a
-- hospital bed, accommodation, maintenance, nursing care and appropriate professional services ...; or (b) a private
-- in-patient, namely, an in-patient -- (i) who is an eligible person (not being a compensable in-patient, nursing home type
-- patient or nursing home type private patient); and (ii) who elects to be treated as a private in-patient; and (iii) [who is
-- given the same] other than professional and dental services provided by a practitioner acting in a private capacity ...; or
-- (c) a compensable in-patient; or (d) an eligible veteran in-patient [a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement]; or (e) a
-- nursing home type patient ... (not being a compensable in-patient or an ineligible patient); or (f) a nursing home type
-- private patient, namely, an eligible person (not being a compensable in-patient) ... who elects to be treated as a nursing
-- home type private patient; or (g) an ineligible in-patient, namely, an in-patient -- (i) who is not an eligible person (other
-- than a person ... to whom ... a declaration made under the Health Insurance Act 1973 (Commonwealth) section 6(2) applies ...);
-- and (ii) who is not a compensable in-patient". cl 12(4): an eligible person "must elect" public or private on admission.
-- The election to be a nursing home type private patient is read from the same public/private election (an inference).
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
GIVETH A `My class`
`the in-patient class of an eligible person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `me`'s `my election`
    WHEN `to be a private patient` THEN
        IF `me`'s `I am a nursing home type patient` THEN `a nursing home type private patient` ELSE `a private in-patient`
    WHEN `to be a public patient` THEN
        IF `me`'s `I am a nursing home type patient` THEN `a nursing home type patient` ELSE `a public in-patient`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
GIVETH A `My class`
`my in-patient class` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I a compensable patient` `me` `as an in-patient` THEN `a compensable in-patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement` THEN `an eligible veteran in-patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973` THEN `the in-patient class of an eligible person` `me`
        IF `me`'s `a declaration under s 6(2) of the Health Insurance Act 1973 applies to me`
            THEN `not classified: the Order gives no in-patient class`
        OTHERWISE `an ineligible in-patient`

-- cl 13(2): a day patient is "(a) a compensable day patient; or (b) an eligible day patient ... (i) who is an eligible person;
-- but (ii) who is not a compensable day patient; or (c) an ineligible day patient" (neither).
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
GIVETH A `My class`
`my day patient class` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I a compensable patient` `me` `as a day patient` THEN `a compensable day patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973` THEN `an eligible day patient`
        OTHERWISE `an ineligible day patient`

-- cl 14(2): an out-patient is "(a) a compensable out-patient; or (b) an eligible veteran out-patient ...; or (c) an eligible
-- out-patient ... (i) who is an eligible person; but (ii) who is not a compensable out-patient or eligible veteran out-patient;
-- or (d) an ineligible out-patient". Paragraphs (e) concessional beneficiary and (f) pensioner matter only for medicines and
-- are asked there.
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
GIVETH A `My class`
`my out-patient class` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I a compensable patient` `me` `as an out-patient` THEN `a compensable out-patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement` THEN `an eligible veteran out-patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973` THEN `an eligible out-patient`
        OTHERWISE `an ineligible out-patient`

-- cl 15(2): a same day patient is "(a) a public same day patient ... an eligible person (not being a compensable same day
-- patient, an eligible veteran same day patient or a same day patient who elects to be treated as a private same day patient);
-- or (b) a private same day patient ... who elects to be treated as a private same day patient; or (c) a compensable same day
-- patient; or (d) an eligible veteran same day patient ...; or (e) an ineligible same day patient".
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
GIVETH A `My class`
`the same day class of an eligible person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `me`'s `my election`
    WHEN `to be a private patient` THEN `a private same day patient`
    WHEN `to be a public patient` THEN `a public same day patient`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
GIVETH A `My class`
`my same day patient class` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I a compensable patient` `me` `as a same day patient` THEN `a compensable same day patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement` THEN `an eligible veteran same day patient`
        IF `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973` THEN `the same day class of an eligible person` `me`
        OTHERWISE `an ineligible same day patient`

@export What class of patient am I for hospital fees and charges (Order cll 6A, 11-15)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
GIVETH A `My class`
`What class of patient am I` MEANS
    IF `Am I free of all fees under cl 6A` `me` `attending`
    THEN `not classified: no fees or charges are payable (cl 6A)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `attending`
         WHEN `as an in-patient`     THEN `my in-patient class` `me`
         WHEN `as a day patient`     THEN `my day patient class` `me`
         WHEN `as an out-patient`    THEN `my out-patient class` `me`
         WHEN `as a same day patient` THEN `my same day patient class` `me`

§§ `Order cll 5, 6 and Schedule 1 Divisions 1 and 2 -- what the hospital charges me`

-- How each charge in Schedule 1 is fixed. "no charge"; a fixed amount ("$467 per day"); a ceiling ("no more than $774 per
-- day"); an amount the Department CEO determines "according to the cost" (cl 10A); nothing fixed by the Order, so the health
-- service provider determines it under s 55(1), consistently with any policy framework (s 55(2)(b)); or no fees at all
-- (cl 6A).
DECLARE `How my charge is fixed` IS ONE OF
    `no charge`
    `a fixed amount`
    `no more than an amount`
    `an amount the Department CEO determines at cost`
    `not fixed by the Order: the provider determines it under s 55`
    `charged per out-patient service, not per day`
    `no fees or charges at all (cl 6A)`

DECLARE `Charge` HAS
    `how it is fixed` IS A `How my charge is fixed`
    `amount`          IS A NUMBER  -- dollars; 0 unless the Order fixes an amount or a ceiling

`nothing to pay` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `no charge`, `amount` IS 0
`no fees under cl 6A` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `no fees or charges at all (cl 6A)`, `amount` IS 0
`not fixed by the Order` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `not fixed by the Order: the provider determines it under s 55`, `amount` IS 0
`at cost` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `an amount the Department CEO determines at cost`, `amount` IS 0
`per service instead` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `charged per out-patient service, not per day`, `amount` IS 0

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Charge`
`a fixed charge of` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `a fixed amount`, `amount` IS `x`

GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Charge`
`a charge of no more than` MEANS `Charge` WITH `how it is fixed` IS `no more than an amount`, `amount` IS `x`

-- Schedule 1 Division 2 Subdivision 1 (compensable in-patients): "1. ... in a hospital bed, except services referred to in item 5
-- or 6 -- $3 529 per day"; "2. [and] 3. ... in a hospital bed for a patient ... in respect of whose health services the Motor
-- Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 applies or prima facie appears to apply -- no charge" (item 3: at Perth Children's
-- Hospital); "4. ... in a nursing home bed -- $385 per day"; "5. ... for a ventilator dependent compensable in-patient with
-- tracheostomy requiring 24 hour a day individual care -- $7 202 per day"; "6. ... for a patient requiring 24 hour a day care
-- for airway management, with or without tracheostomy -- $4 305 per day".
-- Reading: items 2 and 3 cover every hospital-bed stay of a motor-vehicle third-party patient, including one who would
-- otherwise fall in item 5 or 6; item 4 (a nursing home bed) is not excepted for them.
DECLARE `My bed` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary hospital bed`
    `a nursing home bed`
    `a hospital bed, ventilator dependent with tracheostomy and 24-hour individual care`
    `a hospital bed, with 24-hour care for airway management`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient`
      `bed` IS A `My bed`
GIVETH A `Charge`
`the compensable in-patient daily charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `bed`
    WHEN `a nursing home bed` THEN `a fixed charge of` 385
    OTHERWISE
        IF `me`'s `motor vehicle third party insurance applies or appears to apply` THEN `nothing to pay`
        ELSE CONSIDER `bed`
             WHEN `a hospital bed, ventilator dependent with tracheostomy and 24-hour individual care` THEN `a fixed charge of` 7202
             WHEN `a hospital bed, with 24-hour care for airway management` THEN `a fixed charge of` 4305
             OTHERWISE `a fixed charge of` 3529

-- Schedule 1 Division 1 (cl 5). Item 1, "Accommodation, maintenance, nursing care and other services -- (a) for public
-- in-patients: no charge; (b) for private in-patients -- (i) in single bed wards (if taken at patient's request): no more than
-- $774 per day; (ii) in other wards: $467 per day; (c) for nursing home type patients: $82.50 per day; (d) for nursing home type
-- private patients: $239.20 per day; (e) for ineligible in-patients: $3 417 per day; (f) for eligible veteran in-patients: no
-- charge". Item 3, "Accommodation, maintenance and other services for eligible day patients: no charge". Item 6, "Same day health
-- service ... (a) for public same day patients: no charge; (b) for private same day patients: $385 per day; (c) for eligible
-- veteran same day patients: no charge; (d) for ineligible same day patients: $3 258 per day".
-- Division 2 Subdivision 3 (compensable same day patients), item 10: motor vehicle third party "no charge"; "(c) for any other
-- patient: $4 465 per day".
-- Neither Division fixes a charge for a compensable day patient or an ineligible day patient (cl 6(1) applies Division 2 only to
-- compensable in-, out- and same day patients), so the provider determines it under s 55.
@export What does the public hospital charge me per day for my stay (Order cll 5, 6, 6A; Schedule 1 Divisions 1 and 2)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
      `I asked for a single bed ward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a single-bed ward at your own request
      `bed` IS A `My bed` @desc The kind of bed and care (matters only for a compensable in-patient)
GIVETH A `Charge`
`What does the hospital charge me per day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What class of patient am I` `me` `attending`
    WHEN `a public in-patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `a private in-patient` THEN
        IF `I asked for a single bed ward` THEN `a charge of no more than` 774 ELSE `a fixed charge of` 467
    WHEN `a nursing home type patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 82.50
    WHEN `a nursing home type private patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 239.20
    WHEN `an ineligible in-patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 3417
    WHEN `an eligible veteran in-patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `a compensable in-patient` THEN `the compensable in-patient daily charge` `me` `bed`
    WHEN `an eligible day patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `a compensable day patient` THEN `not fixed by the Order`
    WHEN `an ineligible day patient` THEN `not fixed by the Order`
    WHEN `a public same day patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `a private same day patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 385
    WHEN `an eligible veteran same day patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `an ineligible same day patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 3258
    WHEN `a compensable same day patient` THEN
        IF `me`'s `motor vehicle third party insurance applies or appears to apply` THEN `nothing to pay` ELSE `a fixed charge of` 4465
    WHEN `not classified: no fees or charges are payable (cl 6A)` THEN `no fees under cl 6A`
    WHEN `not classified: the Order gives no in-patient class` THEN `not fixed by the Order`
    OTHERWISE `per service instead`

@export What will my whole stay cost me under the Order, in dollars, at most (Order Schedule 1 Divisions 1 and 2)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
      `I asked for a single bed ward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in a single-bed ward at your own request
      `bed` IS A `My bed` @desc The kind of bed and care (matters only for a compensable in-patient)
      `days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days you are charged for
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What will my stay cost under the Order` MEANS
    (`What does the hospital charge me per day` `me` `attending` `I asked for a single bed ward` `bed`)'s `amount` TIMES `days`

§§ `Order Schedule 1 Division 1 items 4, 5, 7; Division 2 items 7-9; cl 10A -- out-patients, medicines, someone staying with me`

-- Division 1 item 4: "Out-patients service, except for medicines referred to in item 5 -- (a) for eligible out-patients and
-- eligible veteran out-patients: no charge; (b) for ineligible out-patients -- for each individual service rendered: $397".
-- Division 2 item 7: "For radiological service -- for each item of service: $397"; item 9: "For each other individual service
-- (with any medicines supplied at the time of the initial service being treated as included in that service): $397".
@export What does the public hospital charge me for each out-patient service (Order Schedule 1 Division 1 item 4, Division 2 items 7, 9)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
GIVETH A `Charge`
`What does the hospital charge me for an out-patient service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What class of patient am I` `me` `as an out-patient`
    WHEN `an eligible out-patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `an eligible veteran out-patient` THEN `nothing to pay`
    WHEN `an ineligible out-patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 397
    WHEN `a compensable out-patient` THEN `a fixed charge of` 397
    OTHERWISE `no fees under cl 6A`

-- Division 1 item 5: "Medicines, for each item -- (a) for holders of an entitlement card: no charge; (b) for other people who
-- are -- (i) veterans who hold a Gold Card or a White Card; or (ii) pensioners; or (iii) concessional beneficiaries: no more than
-- $7.70; (c) for all other people (other than ineligible out-patients): no more than $25". Division 2 item 8 (compensable
-- out-patients): "For medicines, subject to item 9, for each item: no more than $25". cl 10A: for an ineligible in-, out-, day or
-- same day patient, "The charge for the provision of a medicine in a hospital ... is to be of an amount determined by the
-- Department CEO according to the cost of providing the medicine."
-- Reading: cl 5(2)(a) and cl 6(2)(a) each give way to the other Division, so for a compensable out-patient both item 5 and item 8
-- could apply; item 8, the compensable patients' own item, is taken.
-- "entitlement card" is the National Health Act 1953 Part VII term; "pensioner" and "concessional beneficiary" are cl 14(2)(e),
-- (f): borrowed, asked as facts.
DECLARE `My medicine concession` IS ONE OF
    `I hold an entitlement card`
    `I am a Gold or White Card veteran, a pensioner or a concessional beneficiary`
    `none of these`

@export What does the public hospital charge me for each out-patient medicine item (Order Schedule 1 Division 1 item 5, Division 2 item 8, cl 10A)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `concession` IS A `My medicine concession` @desc Whether you hold an entitlement card, or are a Gold or White Card veteran, a pensioner or a concessional beneficiary
GIVETH A `Charge`
`What does the hospital charge me for an out-patient medicine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `What class of patient am I` `me` `as an out-patient`
    WHEN `an ineligible out-patient` THEN `at cost`
    WHEN `a compensable out-patient` THEN `a charge of no more than` 25
    WHEN `not classified: no fees or charges are payable (cl 6A)` THEN `no fees under cl 6A`
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `concession`
        WHEN `I hold an entitlement card` THEN `nothing to pay`
        WHEN `I am a Gold or White Card veteran, a pensioner or a concessional beneficiary` THEN `a charge of no more than` 7.70
        WHEN `none of these` THEN `a charge of no more than` 25

-- Division 1 item 7: "Accommodation for persons accompanying patients (except when parent accompanies sick child for medical
-- wellbeing of sick child or breastfeeding, or when breastfed child accompanies sick mother): $46 per day".
DECLARE `Why I am staying with the patient` IS ONE OF
    `I am a parent with my sick child, for the child's wellbeing or to breastfeed`
    `I am a breastfed child with my sick mother`
    `any other reason`

@export What does the public hospital charge me per day to stay with a patient (Order Schedule 1 Division 1 item 7)?
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why I am staying with the patient` @desc Why you are staying in the hospital with the patient
GIVETH A `Charge`
`What do I pay to stay with a patient` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `any other reason` THEN `a fixed charge of` 46
    OTHERWISE `nothing to pay`

§§ `Order cll 7, 8 and Schedule 1 Divisions 3 and 4 -- an MRI study, a pathology test`

-- cl 7(2): Division 3 applies to an MRI service "provided by, in or at a provider hospital to -- (a) a compensable in-patient; or
-- (b) an ineligible in-patient; or (c) a compensable out-patient; or (d) an ineligible out-patient; or (e) a compensable same day
-- patient; or (f) an ineligible same day patient." A "provider hospital" has MRI equipment for which a Medicare benefit is
-- payable (cl 7(1)). Division 3: "(a) one region of the body: $1 735; (b) 2 contiguous regions: $1 735; (c) 2 or more separate
-- regions: $3 465; (d) 3 or more contiguous regions: $3 465"; item 2: "If Gadolinium used as a contrast medium an additional
-- charge: $205".
-- For anyone else Division 3 fixes nothing; a public in-patient's or eligible out-patient's MRI falls under Division 1's "no
-- charge" for their stay or out-patient service (a reading), which the questions above answer.
DECLARE `My MRI study` IS ONE OF
    `one region of the body`
    `2 contiguous regions`
    `2 or more separate regions`
    `3 or more contiguous regions`

GIVEN `c` IS A `My class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 3 reaches my class` IF
    CONSIDER `c`
    WHEN `a compensable in-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible in-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a compensable out-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible out-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a compensable same day patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible same day patient` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export What does the public hospital charge me for an MRI study (Order cl 7; Schedule 1 Division 3)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
      `the hospital's MRI attracts Medicare benefits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital's MRI equipment is equipment for which a Medicare benefit is payable
      `study` IS A `My MRI study` @desc Which regions of the body are scanned
      `gadolinium used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether gadolinium is used as a contrast medium
GIVETH A `Charge`
`What does the hospital charge me for an MRI study` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I free of all fees under cl 6A` `me` `attending` THEN `no fees under cl 6A`
        IF `the hospital's MRI attracts Medicare benefits` AND `Division 3 reaches my class` (`What class of patient am I` `me` `attending`)
             THEN `a fixed charge of` (`the study charge` PLUS `the contrast charge`)
        OTHERWISE `not fixed by the Order`
    WHERE
        `the study charge` MEANS
            CONSIDER `study`
            WHEN `one region of the body` THEN 1735
            WHEN `2 contiguous regions` THEN 1735
            OTHERWISE 3465
        `the contrast charge` MEANS IF `gadolinium used` THEN 205 ELSE 0

-- cl 8 and Division 4: "MBS amount, for a pathology service, means the amount of the fee specified in the item for that pathology
-- service in the Medicare Benefits Schedule." Item 1: "The MBS amount for the service if the service is provided to -- (a) a
-- private in-patient; or (b) a compensable in-patient; or (c) a nursing home type private patient; or (d) an ineligible
-- in-patient; or (e) a compensable day patient; or (f) an ineligible day patient; or (g) a compensable out-patient; or (h) an
-- ineligible out-patient; or (i) a private same day patient; or (j) a compensable same day patient; or (k) an ineligible same day
-- patient." Item 2: "If the service is provided to a private pathology out-patient -- 85% of the MBS amount".
-- cl 14(3), (4): at the time of the test "an eligible person (not being a compensable patient or a veteran), a concessional
-- beneficiary or a pensioner may elect to be treated as a private pathology out-patient"; then "despite subclause (2)(c), (e) or
-- (f), the person is not classified as an eligible out-patient" for it. The MBS is NOT DEPOSITED: the MBS amount is an input.
-- Reading: "not being ... a veteran" is read as an eligible veteran out-patient (one who elected the DVA arrangement).
GIVEN `c` IS A `My class`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Division 4 item 1 reaches my class` IF
    CONSIDER `c`
    WHEN `a private in-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a compensable in-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a nursing home type private patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible in-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a compensable day patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible day patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a compensable out-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible out-patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a private same day patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a compensable same day patient` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an ineligible same day patient` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export What does the public hospital charge me for a pathology service (Order cll 8, 14(3), (4); Schedule 1 Division 4)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me as a patient` @desc Your Medicare status, any compensation claim, any election you made, and your circumstances
      `attending` IS A `How I attend` @desc Whether you are an in-patient, a day patient, an out-patient or a same day patient
      `I elect to be a private pathology out-patient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, as an out-patient, you chose to be treated privately for this pathology test
      `the MBS amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The Medicare Benefits Schedule fee for the pathology item, in dollars
GIVETH A `Charge`
`What does the hospital charge me for a pathology service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Am I free of all fees under cl 6A` `me` `attending` THEN `no fees under cl 6A`
        IF `I may elect private pathology` AND `I elect to be a private pathology out-patient`
             THEN `a fixed charge of` (`the MBS amount` TIMES 85 DIVIDED BY 100)
        IF `Division 4 item 1 reaches my class` (`What class of patient am I` `me` `attending`)
             THEN `a fixed charge of` `the MBS amount`
        OTHERWISE `not fixed by the Order`
    WHERE
        `I may elect private pathology` MEANS
            CONSIDER `attending`
            WHEN `as an out-patient` THEN
                    `me`'s `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973`
                AND (NOT (`Am I a compensable patient` `me` `as an out-patient`))
                AND (NOT `me`'s `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement`)
            OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `ss 55(2), 57 -- is what I am asked to pay lawful, and do I owe it`

-- s 55(2): "A health service provider must not determine or impose a fee or charge under subsection (1) that is inconsistent with
-- -- (a) an order made under section 56; or (b) any policy framework issued under section 26(2)(e)." The policy frameworks are
-- not deposited: consistency with them is a fact.
@export Is the amount the hospital asks me to pay consistent with the Fees and Charges Order (s 55(2))?
GIVEN `the Order's charge` IS A `Charge` @desc What the Order fixes for the service (the answer to one of the charge questions)
      `asked to pay` IS A NUMBER @desc What the hospital asks you to pay, in dollars, for the same unit (a day, a service, an item)
      `consistent with the policy frameworks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charge is consistent with the Department's policy frameworks on fees (s 26(2)(e))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the charge consistent with the Order` IF
        `consistent with the policy frameworks`
    AND CONSIDER `the Order's charge`'s `how it is fixed`
        WHEN `no charge` THEN `asked to pay` EQUALS 0
        WHEN `no fees or charges at all (cl 6A)` THEN `asked to pay` EQUALS 0
        WHEN `a fixed amount` THEN `asked to pay` EQUALS `the Order's charge`'s `amount`
        WHEN `no more than an amount` THEN `asked to pay` AT MOST `the Order's charge`'s `amount`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 57: "(1) A fee or charge imposed under section 55 is payable by or on behalf of the person who received the health service.
-- (2) A health service provider may waive, or refund, the whole or any part of a fee or charge." The waiver is the provider's
-- choice: asked as a fact.
@export Do I owe the hospital the fee it has imposed, after any waiver (s 57)?
GIVEN `lawfully imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the fee was imposed under s 55 (the hospital may charge you, and the amount is consistent with the Order)
      `the amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The fee imposed, in dollars
      `the amount waived` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of it the hospital has waived or refunded, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much do I owe the hospital` MEANS
    IF `lawfully imposed` AND `the amount` GREATER THAN `the amount waived`
    THEN `the amount` MINUS `the amount waived`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 53A, 53B, 57A, 57C, 57D -- can the hospital take its charge out of my compensation`

-- s 53B(1): compensation is a payment "made in relation to an injury to a person ... that is -- (i) a payment of damages; or (ii) a
-- payment under a scheme of insurance or compensation under a written law or a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory,
-- but not including a payment under such a scheme to which the recipient has contributed; or (iii) a payment ... in settlement of
-- a claim for damages or a claim under an insurance scheme of a kind to which subparagraph (ii) applies; or (iv) any other
-- compensation or damages payment, other than a payment under a scheme to which the recipient has contributed; or (v) a payment
-- of a kind ... prescribed by the regulations; and (b) that is paid or payable after the day on which the Health Services
-- Amendment Act 2023 section 31 comes into operation". That day is 1 July 2023 (compilation table: Part 2 of that Act, SL 2023/103).
-- (2): not "a payment of a kind ... prescribed by the regulations". "injury includes an illness or disease" (s 53A).
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `damages`
    `a payment under a statutory insurance or compensation scheme`
    `a settlement of a claim for damages or under such a scheme`
    `another compensation or damages payment`
    `a payment of a prescribed kind`
    `something else`

@export Is the payment I receive for my injury compensation that the hospital can claim against (s 53B)?
GIVEN `kind` IS A `Kind of payment` @desc What the payment is
      `I contributed to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment comes from a scheme you paid into (for example your own insurance)
      `excluded by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude a payment of this kind (s 53B(2))
      `date paid or payable as YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER @desc When the payment is paid or payable, as a number such as 20290815
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my payment compensation` IF
        `date paid or payable as YYYYMMDD` GREATER THAN 20230701
    AND (NOT `excluded by regulation`)
    AND CONSIDER `kind`
        WHEN `damages` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a payment under a statutory insurance or compensation scheme` THEN NOT `I contributed to the scheme`
        WHEN `a settlement of a claim for damages or under such a scheme` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `another compensation or damages payment` THEN NOT `I contributed to the scheme`
        WHEN `a payment of a prescribed kind` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 57A(1): applies if "(a) a person (a patient) receives a health service from a health service provider in relation to an
-- injury; and (b) the health service provider ... did not charge the patient a compensable charge for the service". (2): "When
-- compensation is paid or payable in relation to an injury for which the patient received a health service, the compensable
-- charge for the health service is payable to the health service provider". (3): it "may recover the compensable charge ...
-- from -- (a) a compensation payer ... if the compensation payer has not paid, or has partially paid, the compensation ...; or
-- (b) the patient if the patient receives compensation in relation to the injury; ...". s 53A: a "compensable charge" is "a fee or
-- charge that a person who received compensation could be charged for the service when the service was provided" -- that is,
-- the Order's compensable-patient rates. s 57C: the provider "may waive, or refund, the whole or any part" (a fact).
@export Can the hospital recover its compensable charge from me out of my compensation (ss 57A, 57C)?
GIVEN `I received the service from a health service provider for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a WA health service provider treated you for the injury or illness
      `I was charged a compensable charge at the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital already charged you at the compensable rate for the service
      `the payment is compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you receive is compensation under s 53B
      `I receive the compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (not only the insurer or other payer) have received compensation for the injury
      `the hospital has waived it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital has waived the compensable charge (s 57C)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the hospital recover the compensable charge from me` IF
        `I received the service from a health service provider for the injury`
    AND (NOT `I was charged a compensable charge at the time`)
    AND `the payment is compensation`
    AND `I receive the compensation`
    AND (NOT `the hospital has waived it`)

-- s 57D: if "(a) a compensation payer has not paid, or has partially paid, compensation to the patient ...; and (b) the health
-- service provider ... has not been paid the compensable charge; and (c) the chief executive of the health service provider has
-- given notice to the compensation payer", then "(2) The compensation payer must pay the compensable charge to the health service
-- provider before paying the compensation to the patient".
@export Must the insurer or other payer pay the hospital before it pays me my compensation (s 57D)?
GIVEN `the payer has not paid me in full` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the insurer or other payer has not yet paid you all the compensation
      `the hospital has not been paid its compensable charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital's compensable charge is still unpaid
      `the hospital's chief executive gave the payer notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the hospital's chief executive has given the payer notice of the charge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the payer pay the hospital before paying me` IF
        `the payer has not paid me in full`
    AND `the hospital has not been paid its compensable charge`
    AND `the hospital's chief executive gave the payer notice`

§§ `ss 34(2)(f), 217, 219, 220 -- what the Act gives me as a patient`

-- s 34(2): "A health service provider also has the following functions -- ... (f) to establish an efficient and effective
-- procedure for dealing with complaints about the provision of health services by the health service provider". The Act states
-- no other right of the patient to a particular standard of care. A function, not a right to a remedy: what it means for me is
-- that a complaints procedure must exist.
@export Must the health service that treats me have a procedure for dealing with my complaint (s 34(2)(f))?
GIVEN `provider` IS A `Who provides my health service` @desc Who gives you the care
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my provider have a complaints procedure` IF
    CONSIDER `provider`
    WHEN `a health service provider` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 219(1): "A person must not (whether directly or indirectly) collect, use or disclose any information obtained by the person
-- because of -- (a) the person's office, position, employment or engagement under or for the purposes of this Act; or (b) any
-- disclosure made to the person under this Act ... Penalty for this subsection: a fine of $5 000." (2): not "statistical or other
-- information that is not personal information". (3): no offence if authorised under s 220(1).
-- s 220(1): authorised "if the information is collected, used or disclosed in good faith in any of these circumstances -- (a)
-- for the purpose of, or in connection with, performing a function under this Act or another written law; (b) for the purposes of
-- section 215 or Division 2; (c) otherwise under this Act ...; (d) under another law; (e) to a court ... in the course of
-- proceedings ...; (f) under an order of a court ...; (g) for the purposes of the investigation of a suspected offence or
-- disciplinary matter ...; (h) if the information ... is personal information -- with the consent of the individual ...; (i) any
-- other circumstances prescribed".
DECLARE `Why my information is disclosed` IS ONE OF
    `to perform a function under this Act or another written law`
    `for the health information system or under Division 2 of Part 17`
    `otherwise under this Act`
    `under another law`
    `to a court in proceedings, or under a court order`
    `to investigate a suspected offence or disciplinary matter, or for those proceedings`
    `with my consent`
    `in a prescribed circumstance`
    `for no such reason`

@export May someone who got my information through the health system collect, use or disclose it (ss 219, 220)?
GIVEN `obtained through the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they got your information through their work under the Act, or through a disclosure made under it
      `it is personal information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information is about you personally (not statistics)
      `why` IS A `Why my information is disclosed` @desc Why they collect, use or disclose it
      `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they act in good faith
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my information be disclosed` IF
        (NOT `obtained through the Act`)
    OR  (NOT `it is personal information`)
    OR  (    `in good faith`
         AND CONSIDER `why`
             WHEN `for no such reason` THEN FALSE
             OTHERWISE TRUE)

-- s 217(2): "The chief executive of a health service provider may, in accordance with the regulations, disclose relevant
-- information about a patient of the health service provider to any person who, in the opinion of the chief executive, has a
-- sufficient interest in the treatment, care, health, safety or wellbeing of the patient." "relevant information" is health
-- information that, "in the opinion of the chief executive", is or is likely to be relevant to the patient's treatment or care,
-- or health, safety or wellbeing (s 217(1)). Both opinions are the chief executive's, asked as facts; my consent is not needed.
@export May the hospital's chief executive tell someone about my health without my consent (s 217)?
GIVEN `the chief executive thinks it relevant to my care or wellbeing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the chief executive's opinion, the information is or is likely to be relevant to your treatment, care, health, safety or wellbeing
      `the chief executive thinks they have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, in the chief executive's opinion, the person told has a sufficient interest in your treatment, care, health, safety or wellbeing
      `in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure follows the regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the chief executive disclose my health information` IF
        `the chief executive thinks it relevant to my care or wellbeing`
    AND `the chief executive thinks they have a sufficient interest`
    AND `in accordance with the regulations`

@export What is the most a person can be fined for wrongly disclosing my information, in dollars (s 219(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most someone can be fined for disclosing my information` MEANS 5000
